00:20:42.000 --> 00:21:21.000
Although irritated at the detective's presence, Christine agreed to answer some routine questions. She led them into her lounge room and to a small table. The detective's attention was immediately drawn to a hooded, waterproof jacket hanging off the back of a chair. It looked identical to the active life one owned by Urban Hoggleen, from which the label had been cut out and left near the Tararoo Creek Road track. Christine agreed to let them have a look at the jacket, explaining that her husband had recently given it to one of their sons.

